      "chapter": "setup",
      "spoken": "A random sample records each student once: how they commute and whether they arrive on time. Test for association.",
      "coach": "Each student is counted once. The rows are Walk, Cycle and Bus; columns are On time and Late.",
      "end": 8.439,
      "hold": 2,
      "keys": []
    },
    {
      "chapter": "setup",
      "spoken": "The null hypothesis says commute mode and arrival status are independent. The alternative is that they are associated. Choose a five percent significance level before testing.",
      "coach": "H₀: commute mode and arrival status are independent. Hₐ: they are associated. Use α = 0.05.",
      "end": 20.995,
      "hold": 2,
      "keys": []
    },
